      "text": "**Evaluating playlist options**\n\nI’m thinking about adding songs to a playlist and questioning whether source details are causing confusion with a delayed query. I need to choose 11 additional songs, and I wonder if there’s a “Select all” option to streamline the process. If I pick the first 11, I might end up with around 12 songs, totaling about 46 minutes. The durations vary, so I’ll need to check the task data to get a better estimate. I'll track details through the UI.\n\n**Calculating song selection process**\n\nI'm looking at using XPath to click and gather 11 title names, which requires some interactions. I think the app's budget counts each step, and I still have a few left for other actions. Selecting these songs should give me 12 total, but I may need to verify everything isn’t overlaid. The first 12 titles include \"Silent Dreams,\" but I need to check if I can click them despite some overlapping elements. Selecting the first 10 titles up through “Moonlight Sonata” might get me close to my goal.\n\n**Counting song selections**\n\nI’m counting the songs I’ve selected so far: \"City,\" \"Endless,\" \"Eternal,\" \"Falling,\" \"Forever,\" \"Golden,\" \"Heartbeat,\" \"Hidden,\" and \"Moonlight.\" I still need two more. \"Return to Paradise\" is partly visible, but scrolling to select more would add an extra step. Selecting just 10 songs gives a duration of about 38-42 minutes, which feels too short since I aim for 12. I might consider using the “Select all” option from the menu but worry about the risk of having too many songs in the library.\n\n",
